        "evidence": "the negative obligation of this Boolean verification reads -off(lamp) at W0+2; -off is written at step 1 and step 2 writes off only under a condition, so a No would need the negative carried, and the starting backend has none. A Yes needs no carried negative: the requirement has polarities [negative], the query runs, and the answer policy keeps the Yes and refuses every other answer. at W0 off(lamp) holds and on(lamp) is unknown (no fact); S4's condition is true and S5's is not established, so only S4 applies at step 1: on(lamp) written, off(lamp) removed with a marker. At W0+1 on(lamp) holds and -off(lamp) is explicit, so at step 2 only S5 applies. Each effect sees the predecessor only: S5 does not read S4's write in the same step (A5.1). Not established is not false: S5 does not apply at step 1 because its condition lacks positive support, not because on(lamp) was refuted."
